{
 "id": "analogy_search",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "shape_vocabulary"
 ],
 "description": "THE ANALOGY SEARCH AS A FIRST-CLASS GRAPH SEED \u2014 SHAPE_AUDIT.md \u00a72.4. domains/analogical_thinking.py::find_analogies was 'never moved into the graph': a Python triple-nested loop over concept pairs scoring a set overlap of string tokens at five fixed orders, 'not one of which consults a concept's edges'. This seed makes the search a run_rules fixpoint one grain over from seeds/meta_shape_growth.json / problem_shape_growth.json, with ZERO new Rust (every decision is an existing generic Term, the same choice problem_shape_growth made): ap_decode runs the UNCHANGED ShapeDecode Term over a per-field-scoped ConceptShape codebook (the cross-field scan, in Rust, over ARBITRARY concept structure \u2014 relational edges when present, attrs + vocabulary axes otherwise); ap_match derives shared structure via FixedCount(AntiUnify(...)); ap_systematic fires the parallelogram as a Count(Filter(Eq(transform_key))) recurrence verdict; ap_emit writes an Analogy node + implements edge ONLY when aligned or corroborated. Emitted by tools/build_analogy_search_seed.py. Ingest: domains/analogy_search.observe.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "analogy_search",
  "description": "the analogy search decodes each source concept against other fields' concept shapes and grows analogies on aligned or corroborated structure; tick-driven, no Python loop"
 },
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [
